## FAQs

Do I need to book in advance? Nope. Walk-ins are welcome at 546 Yates St anytime. If you have a specific time in mind or you're bringing a larger group, booking online at infusion-play.com helps secure your slot.

What is the Challenge + Immersion bundle? A package that combines the VR Arena and the Interactive Play rooms into a single visit. It's the best way to experience both formats back-to-back, and it's popular with couples, friend groups, and corporate teams.

Is Infusion Play suitable for children? Kids aged 8 and up can jump into the VR Arena and Interactive Play rooms. For children under 8, the sister location Infusion XR Arcade offers room-scale VR at a more appropriate pace and intensity.

What VR games are available? The VR Arena runs After the Fall and Arizona Sunshine — both multiplayer-capable, free-roaming zombie shooters with rifle-style controllers. This is full-body VR, not seated or stationary play.

How long does a typical visit last? A single activity session runs around one hour. The Challenge + Immersion bundle, combining VR and physical challenge rooms, runs approximately one to two hours depending on your group size and pace.

Can Infusion Play host large corporate groups or events? Yes. The venue accommodates groups of 30 or more and has food and beverages on-site, making it a practical full-event solution without coordinating multiple locations. Booking ahead is recommended for large groups.

Is Infusion Play new to Victoria? The 546 Yates St location opened June 16, 2026, but Infusion Play has been part of Victoria since 2016. New flagship space — not a new business.

